vironment for Democrats keep Bottoms within striking distance, leaving the race a tossup with a slight Republican tilt.", "watch": "Scrutiny of Jackson's business empire, his debate absences, or a late shift in the national environment could move a race this tight before early voting concludes.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Open seat: Brian Kemp (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Georgia's governorship is open as Republican Brian Kemp terms out, and the contest between Democrat Keisha Lance Bottoms and Republican Rick Jackson sits close to even. Seven race raters call it a Tossup, with one rating it a slight Democratic edge. Polling since mid-September shows Jackson ahead by one to three points, a shift from midsummer surveys that favored Bottoms, though several recent polls come from Republican-leaning sponsors. Prediction markets put Democratic win odds in the mid-40s.\n\nMoney is the race's clearest asymmetry: Jackson, whose multibillion-dollar business empire has drawn press scrutiny, has raised roughly $119 million to Bottoms' $5.8 million. Jackson has campaigned with Kemp and skipped some debates, leaving Bottoms alone on stage. Early voting is underway with both campaigns pushing turnout, and the outcome will likely hinge on which side's base shows up in a slightly Republican-leaning state.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.6414, "margin": 1.75}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.5561, "margin": 0.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.5612, "margin": 0.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.5894, "margin": 0.8}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.5413, "margin": 0.8}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.5396, "margin": 0.8}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.5736, "margin": 0.8}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.463, "margin": -0.7}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.5513, "margin": 0.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.5602, "margin": 0.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.4361, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.